<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Proof</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Support Contraction to <math id="A1.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide a short proof that, under the reward-maximization objective in Eq.(<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 preliminary ‣ 2 What is high-quality exploration in RLVR? ‣ Selective Expert Guidance For Effective and Diverse Exploration in Reinforcement Learning of LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), the optimal distribution places all probability mass on <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed question <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\tau)\equiv R(q,\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\tau)\equiv R(q,\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> on the discrete set <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{q}=\operatorname{supp}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{q}=\operatorname{supp}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q))</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\max}=\sup_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}R(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\max}=\sup_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}R(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the set of maximizers by <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\star}=\{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}:R(\tau)=R_{\max}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\star}=\{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}:R(\tau)=R_{\max}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the learning objective in Eq.(<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 preliminary ‣ 2 What is high-quality exploration in RLVR? ‣ Selective Expert Guidance For Effective and Diverse Exploration in Reinforcement Learning of LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is to maximize expected reward but the exact optimal distribution is unknown, we adopt a Maximum Entropy Principle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jaynes, 1957</a>)</cite>. Specifically, we optimize over all probability mass functions <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:\mathcal{S}_{q}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:\mathcal{S}_{q}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{P}\;H(P)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)R(\tau)=C,\ \ \sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>P</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{P}\;H(P)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)R(\tau)=C,\ \ \sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(P)=-\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)\log P(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)=-\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}P(\tau)\log P(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the target expected reward. A standard Lagrangian calculation yields the unique Gibbs-form solution</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\lambda}(\tau)=\frac{\exp\{\lambda R(\tau)\}}{Z(\lambda)},\qquad Z(\lambda)=\sum_{\tau^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}\exp\{\lambda R(\tau^{\prime})\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\lambda}(\tau)=\frac{\exp\{\lambda R(\tau)\}}{Z(\lambda)},\qquad Z(\lambda)=\sum_{\tau^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{q}}\exp\{\lambda R(\tau^{\prime})\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">for some multiplier <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> chosen such that <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{\lambda}}[R]=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{\lambda}}[R]=C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\lambda)=\sum_{\tau}P_{\lambda}(\tau)R(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\lambda)=\sum_{\tau}P_{\lambda}(\tau)R(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}(\lambda)=\operatorname{Var}_{P_{\lambda}}[R]\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}(\lambda)=\operatorname{Var}_{P_{\lambda}}[R]\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing. Moreover, <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\lambda\to\infty}\phi(\lambda)=R_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\lambda\to\infty}\phi(\lambda)=R_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence as <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\uparrow R_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\uparrow R_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and for any <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\notin\mathcal{T}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\notin\mathcal{T}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\star}\in\mathcal{T}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\star}\in\mathcal{T}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{\lambda}(\tau)}{P_{\lambda}(\tau^{\star})}=\exp\{-\lambda\,(R_{\max}-R(\tau))\}\ \longrightarrow\ 0\quad(\lambda\to\infty)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{\lambda}(\tau)}{P_{\lambda}(\tau^{\star})}=\exp\{-\lambda\,(R_{\max}-R(\tau))\}\ \longrightarrow\ 0\quad(\lambda\to\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus all probability mass concentrates on <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> in the limit.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Unbiasedness for Mixed-Policy Rollout</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unbiasedness of speculative sampling is well established in prior work. For completeness, we include a concise proof specialized to our mixed policy <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{mix}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{mix}}</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming that the validation procedure remains unbiased in our setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let the token space be <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and fix a prefix <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the base policy by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{t}(\cdot)=\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,y_{&lt;t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\cdot)=\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,y_{&lt;t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{t}(\cdot)=\pi^{*}(\cdot\mid q,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}(\cdot)=\pi^{*}(\cdot\mid q,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> be the expert policy. The mixed policy is obtained by a deterministic ensemble of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{t},s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{t},s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot)=\pi_{\text{mix}}(\cdot\mid q,y_{&lt;t})=\mathcal{M}\!\big(p_{t}(\cdot),s_{t}(\cdot)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.031em;" width="1.031em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot)=\pi_{\text{mix}}(\cdot\mid q,y_{&lt;t})=\mathcal{M}\!\big(p_{t}(\cdot),s_{t}(\cdot)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes any tokenwise mixing operator that yields a valid distribution on <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., convex mixing). The validation procedure only depends on <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At step <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, a candidate token <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is first sampled from <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is accepted with probability</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}(\tilde{y}_{t})=\min\!\Big(1,\frac{q_{t}(\tilde{y}_{t})}{p_{t}(\tilde{y}_{t})}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}(\tilde{y}_{t})=\min\!\Big(1,\frac{q_{t}(\tilde{y}_{t})}{p_{t}(\tilde{y}_{t})}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">If rejection occurs, a new token is drawn from the residual distribution on <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined for the dummy variable <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(z)=\frac{(q_{t}(z)-p_{t}(z))_{+}}{\sum_{z^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}}(q_{t}(z^{\prime})-p_{t}(z^{\prime}))_{+}},\qquad(u)_{+}=\max\{u,0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(z)=\frac{(q_{t}(z)-p_{t}(z))_{+}}{\sum_{z^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}}(q_{t}(z^{\prime})-p_{t}(z^{\prime}))_{+}},\qquad(u)_{+}=\max\{u,0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For any possible token <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability that it becomes the committed token is therefore</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{t}=v)=p_{t}(x)\min\!\Big(1,\tfrac{q_{t}(v)}{p_{t}(v)}\Big)+\mathbb{P}(\text{reject})\,r_{t}(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>reject</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{t}=v)=p_{t}(x)\min\!\Big(1,\tfrac{q_{t}(v)}{p_{t}(v)}\Big)+\mathbb{P}(\text{reject})\,r_{t}(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The first term equals <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\{p_{t}(v),q_{t}(v)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\{p_{t}(v),q_{t}(v)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The rejection probability is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\text{reject})=1-\sum_{z\in\mathcal{V}}p_{t}(z)\min\!\Big(1,\tfrac{q_{t}(z)}{p_{t}(z)}\Big)=1-\sum_{z\in\mathcal{V}}\min\{p_{t}(z),q_{t}(z)\}=\sum_{z\in\mathcal{V}}(q_{t}(z)-p_{t}(z))_{+}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>reject</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\text{reject})=1-\sum_{z\in\mathcal{V}}p_{t}(z)\min\!\Big(1,\tfrac{q_{t}(z)}{p_{t}(z)}\Big)=1-\sum_{z\in\mathcal{V}}\min\{p_{t}(z),q_{t}(z)\}=\sum_{z\in\mathcal{V}}(q_{t}(z)-p_{t}(z))_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">which coincides with the denominator of <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the second term contributes exactly <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{t}(v)-p_{t}(v))_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{t}(v)-p_{t}(v))_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the two contributions yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{t}=v)=\min\{p_{t}(v),q_{t}(v)\}+(q_{t}(v)-p_{t}(v))_{+}=q_{t}(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{t}=v)=\min\{p_{t}(v),q_{t}(v)\}+(q_{t}(v)-p_{t}(v))_{+}=q_{t}(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Thus the distribution of the validated token is exactly the mixed policy <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To extend the result to entire speculative sequences, note that at <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> the marginal distribution is <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose inductively that the joint distribution of the prefix <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{&lt;t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{&lt;t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j&lt;t}q_{j}(y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j&lt;t}q_{j}(y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditioning on such a prefix, the above calculation shows that <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}\sim q_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}\sim q_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, by induction,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y_{1:T}\mid q)=\prod_{t=1}^{T}q_{t}(y_{t})=\prod_{t=1}^{T}\pi_{\text{mix}}(y_{t}\mid q,y_{&lt;t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y_{1:T}\mid q)=\prod_{t=1}^{T}q_{t}(y_{t})=\prod_{t=1}^{T}\pi_{\text{mix}}(y_{t}\mid q,y_{&lt;t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which is identical to direct autoregressive sampling from the mixed policy.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Platform.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All of our experiments are conducted on workstations equipped with eight NVIDIA A100 GPUs with 80GB memory, running Ubuntu 22.04.4 LTS and CUDA 12.4.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">System Prompt.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models trained under MENTOR and other baselines, except QuestA, share the same system prompt for both training and inference:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="149.65" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 600 149.65" width="600"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,149.65) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.11 L 0 148.54 C 0 149.15 0.5 149.65 1.11 149.65 L 598.89 149.65 C 599.5 149.65 600 149.15 600 148.54 L 600 1.11 C 600 0.5 599.5 0 598.89 0 L 1.11 0 C 0.5 0 0 0.5 0 1.11 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1.11 L 1.11 148.54 L 598.89 148.54 L 598.89 1.11 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.96 11.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:41.63em;--ltx-fo-height:9.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="125.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 125.73)" width="576.04"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:41.63em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a helpful AI Assistant that provides well-reasoned and detailed responses. You FIRST think about the reasoning process as an internal monologue and then provide the final answer. The reasoning process MUST BE enclosed within &lt;think&gt;&lt;/think&gt;tags. The final answer MUST BE put in \boxed{}.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{QUESTION}</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assistant<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For QuestA, we additionally append “## Hint: Partial Solution” after the QUESTION as a hint section.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward Setting.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For outcome reward, we employ Math-Verify to automatically check whether the final answer inside the “&lt;think&gt;… &lt;/think&gt;… \boxed{}” format matches the ground truth, assigning +1 if correct and 0 otherwise. In addition, we introduce a format reward that grants +1 when the response adheres to this format, and 0 if not. The same reward design is applied to MENTOR and all baselines to ensure fairness. For Qwen2.5-7B and Qwen2.5-3B, the weights of outcome reward and format reward are set to 9:1. For LLaMa3.1-8B, however, this ratio is adjusted to 8:2, since the original weighting did not sufficiently enforce format adherence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset Details.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Qwen2.5-7B and Qwen2.5-3B, we use problems from the MATH dataset with difficulty levels 3–5, removing all instances that overlap with the test sets to avoid data leakage. This yields a total of 8,889 training examples. However, for LLaMA3.1-8B, this dataset is too difficult, making the vanilla GRPO algorithm hard to apply. To address this issue, we constructed an easier training set from OpenR1-Math-220K by selecting problems with response lengths shorter than 4K tokens, on which the model could be successfully trained using GRPO. All subsequent methods on LLaMA3.1-8B were trained using this simplified dataset. For each problem, the fixed expert trajectory used in LUFFY and QuestA is generated by DeepSeek-R1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Export Model Details.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Qwen2.5, We adopt OpenR1-Qwen-7B<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            https://huggingface.co/open-r1/OpenR1-Qwen-7B</span></span></span> as the expert model in MENTOR, which is trained on a distilled dataset generated by DeepSeek-R1. For LLaMA3.1, the expert model in MENTOR is obtained by further fine-tuning LLaMA3.1-8B-Instruct under the same dataset and setting used for OpenR1-Qwen-7B.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Details.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct all experiments using the EasyR1<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            https://github.com/hiyouga/EasyR1</span></span></span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite> framework, which employs Verl <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheng et al., 2024</a>)</cite> as the RL training engine and vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2023</a>)</cite> as the rollout engine. The training setup includes a rollout batch of 128, a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, a generation temperature of 1.0, and a higher-clip of 0.28. Each response sequence is up to 8k tokens in length. We perform 8 rollouts per prompt and do not apply KL divergence or entropy regularization (KL Coeff = 0, entropy loss = 0). The mini-batch size is set to 64. For important parameters of MENTOR, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to 1 and annealed to 0 with a cosine schedule over 120 steps, enabling a smooth transition from expert guidance to autonomous exploration. The number of mixed-policy rollouts is set to 4. For <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mtext>p</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>, p is chosen as 0.95, corresponding to the 95-th percentile of token-level entropies within each batch. As a special case, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mtext>p</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to 999 at the first step.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Case Study</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To complement the aggregate analysis in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.4 The Analysis of Reasoning Pattern ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Selective Expert Guidance For Effective and Diverse Exploration in Reinforcement Learning of LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we provide representative trajectory-level cases in this section. These examples illustrate how different training methods influence the emergence of reasoning tokens such as <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verify</span>, <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">check</span>, and <span id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">wait</span>. By examining full reasoning traces, we highlight qualitative differences between methods, offering additional context to the quantitative analysis in the main text.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We find that the incorporation of expert policy indeed shapes the final reasoning patterns of the models, with different methods leading to distinct outcomes.</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">From a stylistic perspective,</span> QuestA and MENTOR exhibit reasoning traces more aligned with on-policy RL, whereas LUFFY shows a closer resemblance to the expert’s style. This difference arises because LUFFY emphasizes direct imitation of expert demonstrations, often reproducing surface-level tokens such as <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">wait</span> and <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">okay</span>, while QuestA and MENTOR encourage the model to explore autonomously while using expert guidance, thereby preserving a degree of its own stylistic characteristics.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">From a content perspective,</span> MENTOR and LUFFY successfully acquire specific reasoning modes from the expert, such as the use of <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verify</span>, which are absent in the base model. In contrast, QuestA, despite leveraging expert policy, does not exhibit the adoption of <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verify</span>. Our analysis suggests this limitation stems from the design choice of using only the first half of the expert trajectory as hints, while tokens like <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verify</span> typically appear toward the end of trajectories, thereby restricting their adoption.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="728.72" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 600 728.72" width="600"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,728.72) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 722.82 C 0 726.08 2.64 728.72 5.91 728.72 L 594.09 728.72 C 597.36 728.72 600 726.08 600 722.82 L 600 5.91 C 600 2.64 597.36 0 594.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 704.61 L 598.03 704.61 L 598.03 5.91 C 598.03 3.73 596.27 1.97 594.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 713.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">An example of On-policy RL</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:49.07em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="679.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 679.03)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">QUESTION<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{3}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{3},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be real numbers such that</span></span>
<span id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A3.Ex10"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=9," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex11"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=16," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex12"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=25." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RESPONSE<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve for <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we start by defining the determinant of the matrix:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The determinant <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> can be expanded as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=x_{1}\begin{vmatrix}y_{2}&amp;1\\
y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}-y_{1}\begin{vmatrix}x_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}+\begin{vmatrix}x_{2}&amp;y_{2}\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}\end{vmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=x_{1}\begin{vmatrix}y_{2}&amp;1\\
y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}-y_{1}\begin{vmatrix}x_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}+\begin{vmatrix}x_{2}&amp;y_{2}\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}\end{vmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This expands to:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})-y_{1}(x_{2}-x_{3})+(x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})-y_{1}(x_{2}-x_{3})+(x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, we have:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=x_{1}y_{2}-x_{1}y_{3}-y_{1}x_{2}+y_{1}x_{3}+x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=x_{1}y_{2}-x_{1}y_{3}-y_{1}x_{2}+y_{1}x_{3}+x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We need to find <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. To do this, we will use the given distances between the points <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. The distances are:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">These distances suggest that the points <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> form a right triangle with sides of lengths 3, 4, and 5. Without loss of generality, we can place the points in a coordinate system where the distances are satisfied. One possible configuration is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})=(0,0),\quad(x_{2},y_{2})=(3,0),\quad(x_{3},y_{3})=(0,4)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})=(0,0),\quad(x_{2},y_{2})=(3,0),\quad(x_{3},y_{3})=(0,4).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, we calculate the determinant <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> for these points:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\begin{vmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;1\\
3&amp;0&amp;1\\
0&amp;4&amp;1\end{vmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\begin{vmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;1\\
3&amp;0&amp;1\\
0&amp;4&amp;1\end{vmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Expanding this determinant, we get:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=0\cdot\begin{vmatrix}0&amp;1\\
4&amp;1\end{vmatrix}-0\cdot\begin{vmatrix}3&amp;1\\
0&amp;1\end{vmatrix}+1\cdot\begin{vmatrix}3&amp;0\\
0&amp;4\end{vmatrix}=1\cdot(3\cdot 4-0\cdot 0)=12." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=0\cdot\begin{vmatrix}0&amp;1\\
4&amp;1\end{vmatrix}-0\cdot\begin{vmatrix}3&amp;1\\
0&amp;1\end{vmatrix}+1\cdot\begin{vmatrix}3&amp;0\\
0&amp;4\end{vmatrix}=1\cdot(3\cdot 4-0\cdot 0)=12.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=12</annotation></semantics></math>, and we need to find <math id="A3.p3.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}=12^{2}=144." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}=12^{2}=144.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, the answer is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{144}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></menclose><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{144}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.p3.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{144}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{144}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1053.08" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 600 1053.08" width="600"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1053.08) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1047.18 C 0 1050.44 2.64 1053.08 5.91 1053.08 L 594.09 1053.08 C 597.36 1053.08 600 1050.44 600 1047.18 L 600 5.91 C 600 2.64 597.36 0 594.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1028.97 L 598.03 1028.97 L 598.03 5.91 C 598.03 3.73 596.27 1.97 594.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1037.57)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">An example of MENTOR</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:72.52em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="1003.39" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1003.39)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">QUESTION<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{3}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{3},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be real numbers such that</span></span>
<span id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A3.Ex26"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=9," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex27"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=16," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex28"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=25." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RESPONSE<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we start by recalling that the determinant of the given matrix is the area of the triangle formed by the points <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> multiplied by 2. Let’s denote the determinant by <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the square of the area of the triangle.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of the triangle can be found using the formula for the area of a triangle with vertices <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\tfrac{1}{2}\left|x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})+x_{2}(y_{3}-y_{1})+x_{3}(y_{1}-y_{2})\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\tfrac{1}{2}\left|x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})+x_{2}(y_{3}-y_{1})+x_{3}(y_{1}-y_{2})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}=4A^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}=4A^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. To find <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to use the given distances between the points. The distances are given by the equations:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">These equations represent the squared lengths of the sides of the triangle. Let’s denote the points as <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. The distances <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=5</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which suggests that triangle <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> is a right triangle with <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle A=90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle A=90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">To verify</span><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.10.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, let’s use the coordinates to check if the points form a right triangle. Assume <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. The squared distances are:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB^{2}=(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB^{2}=(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC^{2}=(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC^{2}=(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC^{2}=(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC^{2}=(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the triangle is indeed a right triangle with <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle A=90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle A=90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of a right triangle is given by half the product of the legs:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\tfrac{1}{2}\times AB\times AC=\tfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\tfrac{1}{2}\times AB\times AC=\tfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}=4A^{2}=4\times 6^{2}=144" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}=4A^{2}=4\times 6^{2}=144</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, the answer is <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{144}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{144}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we start by recalling that the determinant of the matrix is the area of the triangle formed by the points <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> multiplied by 2. Let’s denote the determinant by <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the square of the area of the triangle.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the distances between the points:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">we recognize these as the squared lengths of the sides of a triangle with sides <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=5</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the triangle is a right triangle with <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle A=90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle A=90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of a right triangle is given by:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\tfrac{1}{2}\times AB\times AC=\tfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\tfrac{1}{2}\times AB\times AC=\tfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The determinant <math id="A3.p4.pic1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is twice the area of the triangle:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=2A=12." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=2A=12.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore,</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}=12^{2}=144." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}=12^{2}=144.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, the final answer is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{144}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></menclose><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{144}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="926.55" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 600 926.55" width="600"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,926.55) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 920.64 C 0 923.9 2.64 926.55 5.91 926.55 L 594.09 926.55 C 597.36 926.55 600 923.9 600 920.64 L 600 5.91 C 600 2.64 597.36 0 594.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 902.44 L 598.03 902.44 L 598.03 5.91 C 598.03 3.73 596.27 1.97 594.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 911.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">An example of LUFFY</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:63.18em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="876.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 874.17)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">QUESTION<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{3}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{3},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be real numbers such that</span></span>
<span id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A3.Ex45"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=9," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex46"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=16," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex47"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=25." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RESPONSE<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Okay, so I’ve got this problem here about finding the square of the determinant of a matrix given some conditions on the coordinates. Let me try to break it down step by step.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, the problem gives me six real numbers: <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2},y_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2},y_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. It also provides three equations involving these numbers:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9</annotation></semantics></math>
2. <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16</annotation></semantics></math>
3. <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I need to find the square of the determinant of the matrix:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hmm, okay. Let me recall that the determinant of a 3x3 matrix can be calculated using the formula:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{det}=x_{1}(y_{2}\cdot 1-y_{3}\cdot 1)-y_{1}(x_{2}\cdot 1-x_{3}\cdot 1)+1(x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">det</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{det}=x_{1}(y_{2}\cdot 1-y_{3}\cdot 1)-y_{1}(x_{2}\cdot 1-x_{3}\cdot 1)+1(x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Simplifying that, it becomes:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{det}=x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})-y_{1}(x_{2}-x_{3})+x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">det</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{det}=x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})-y_{1}(x_{2}-x_{3})+x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, the square of the determinant is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{det}^{2}=[x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})-y_{1}(x_{2}-x_{3})+x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}]^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">det</mtext><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{det}^{2}=[x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})-y_{1}(x_{2}-x_{3})+x_{2}y_{3}-x_{3}y_{2}]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">But wait, maybe there’s a better way to approach this. I remember that the determinant of a matrix formed by coordinates of points in a plane is related to the area of the triangle formed by those points. Specifically, the absolute value of the determinant is twice the area of the triangle. So, perhaps I can use that.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let me denote the points as <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. The determinant is twice the area of triangle ABC. So, if I can find the area, I can square it.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area of triangle ABC can be found using the formula:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\left|x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})+x_{2}(y_{3}-y_{1})+x_{3}(y_{1}-y_{2})\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\left|x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})+x_{2}(y_{3}-y_{1})+x_{3}(y_{1}-y_{2})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">But wait, that’s the same as the determinant divided by 2. So, the determinant is twice the area. Therefore, the square of the determinant is four times the square of the area.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, I need to find the area of triangle ABC. Let me denote the area as <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the square of the determinant is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4A^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4A^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, the area <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> can be found using the distance formula. The three given equations are the squared distances between the points. Let me denote the points as <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. So, <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB^{2}=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB^{2}=9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC^{2}=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC^{2}=16</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC^{2}=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC^{2}=25</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=5</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hmm, interesting. So, the sides of the triangle are 3, 4, and 5. That’s a right triangle because <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{2}+4^{2}=5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, the area of a right triangle is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\times\text{base}\times\text{height}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">base</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">height</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\times\text{base}\times\text{height}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the base and height are 3 and 4, so the area is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, the square of the area is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6^{2}=36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6^{2}=36</annotation></semantics></math>. So, the square of the determinant is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 36=144" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">36</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 36=144</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Wait, let me <span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">double-check</span>. The area is 6, so the determinant squared is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 6^{2}=4\times 36=144" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">36</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 6^{2}=4\times 36=144</annotation></semantics></math>. That seems correct.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">But let me make sure I didn’t make a mistake in the area calculation. The sides are 3, 4, 5, which form a right triangle. The area is indeed <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\times 3\times 4=6</annotation></semantics></math>. So, the square is 36, and the determinant squared is 144.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I think that’s it. So, the final answer is 144.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.25.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The square of the determinant is <math id="A3.p5.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{144}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{144}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="869.93" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 600 869.93" width="600"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,869.93) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 864.03 C 0 867.29 2.64 869.93 5.91 869.93 L 594.09 869.93 C 597.36 869.93 600 867.29 600 864.03 L 600 5.91 C 600 2.64 597.36 0 594.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 845.82 L 598.03 845.82 L 598.03 5.91 C 598.03 3.73 596.27 1.97 594.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 854.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">An example of QuestA</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.23em;--ltx-fo-height:59.28em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="820.24" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 820.24)" width="556.67"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.23em;">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">QUESTION<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{3}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{3},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be real numbers such that</span></span>
<span id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A3.Ex54"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=9," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex55"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=16," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex56"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=25." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RESPONSE<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the equations:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{2})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{2})^{2}=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{1}-y_{3})^{2}=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2}-x_{3})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{3})^{2}=25,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">we need to find <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let’s denote the determinant by <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\begin{vmatrix}x_{1}&amp;y_{1}&amp;1\\
x_{2}&amp;y_{2}&amp;1\\
x_{3}&amp;y_{3}&amp;1\end{vmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The square of the determinant <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be found using the formula for the square of a determinant of a <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> matrix. However, we can use a geometric interpretation to simplify the problem.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consider the points <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> in the coordinate plane. The given equations represent the squared distances between these points:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB^{2}=9," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB^{2}=9,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC^{2}=16," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC^{2}=16,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC^{2}=25." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC^{2}=25.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">These distances suggest that the points <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> form a right triangle with <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> as the hypotenuse. This is because <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9+16=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9+16=25</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies the Pythagorean theorem.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Without loss of generality, let’s assume <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the right angle, so <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> form a right triangle with <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> as the hypotenuse. This assumption simplifies our calculations.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area of the triangle <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated using the distances given. The area <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of a triangle with vertices <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{3},y_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{3},y_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> can also be found using the determinant formula for the area of a triangle:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\frac{1}{2}\left|x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})+x_{2}(y_{3}-y_{1})+x_{3}(y_{1}-y_{2})\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\frac{1}{2}\left|x_{1}(y_{2}-y_{3})+x_{2}(y_{3}-y_{1})+x_{3}(y_{1}-y_{2})\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The square of the determinant <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is related to the area of the triangle. Specifically, the square of the determinant of the matrix formed by the coordinates of the points is four times the square of the area of the triangle:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}=4K^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}=4K^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the fact that the points form a right triangle. The legs of the triangle are the distances <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math>, and the hypotenuse is <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math>. The area <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of the right triangle can be calculated as:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\frac{1}{2}\cdot AB\cdot AC=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\sqrt{9}\cdot\sqrt{16}=\frac{1}{2}\cdot 3\cdot 4=\frac{1}{2}\cdot 12=6." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\frac{1}{2}\cdot AB\cdot AC=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\sqrt{9}\cdot\sqrt{16}=\frac{1}{2}\cdot 3\cdot 4=\frac{1}{2}\cdot 12=6.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, the square of the area <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{2}=6^{2}=36." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">36</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{2}=6^{2}=36.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, the square of the determinant <math id="A3.p6.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}=4K^{2}=4\cdot 36=144." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">36</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}=4K^{2}=4\cdot 36=144.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The final answer is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{144}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn></menclose><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{144}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
